  {
   "id": "fy27-cr-deadline",
   "pillar": "top",
   "continuing": true,
   "headline": "Funding runs out December 11, and the budget fight now lands in the lame duck",
   "dek": "The stopgap law signed in September keeps agencies open for ten weeks; the real decisions on next year's spending wait until after the midterms.",
   "whatsNew": [
    "The Continuing Appropriations Act, 2027 funds federal agencies covered by all 12 regular appropriations bills from October 1 through December 11, 2026. [[c1]] The House cleared the final version 370 to 48 on September 1, and the President signed it the next day. [[c2]]"
   ],
   "whyItMatters": [
    "A continuing resolution freezes spending at the previous year's levels. It postpones every choice Congress has not made on the 12 annual spending bills, including defense, until a session in which some members will already have lost their seats. [[c3]]"
   ],
   "whatsNext": [
    "Unless Congress passes full-year bills or another stopgap by December 11, a lapse in appropriations begins. [Sample: next procedural step would come from verified schedules.]"
   ],
   "background": [
    "Continuing resolutions are named after the joint resolutions in which they were historically enacted. This one was passed as a bill, H.R. 6500. [[c4]]"
   ],
   "words": 1180,
   "readingMinutes": 6,
   "status": "verified",
   "claims": [
    {
     "id": "c1",
     "text": "The CR funds agencies under all 12 bills through December 11, 2026.",
     "weight": "core",
     "status": "verified",
     "origin": "agent",
     "evidence": [
